|~ `::legend`, the kind of the legend of a value, and what is declared
   under it: its print, the print of the value it tells laid out by the
   kind of that value.
   The rules it holds: [QSPRN#legend]. ~|

:legend
  |~~ A legend tells a value: it prints as the print of the value laid out
      by its kind, each part the kind reads by a key or an index on a line
      of its own beside the gloss of its page, so a host prints it as it
      prints any answer, its comments painted as comments, and the text
      read back is the value it tells.
      `"~{" | parse !| legend` tells the error at rest of a parse, and
      `payload` answers the value told.
      ::link~(::any/legend | doc) ::link~(::any/print | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts |~~ The value the legend tells. ~~|
    | proves :printsAsTheValueItTellsLaidOut
        |~~ A legend prints as the value it tells, read back as that value.
        ~~|
        ~(::point[0 1 2] | :p it | legend | print | parse | open | eq p)
    | proves :answersTheValueItTellsByPayload
        |~~ `payload` answers the value a legend tells. ~~|
        ~([1 2] | legend | payload | eq [1 2])

:legend/print
  |~~ Answers the print of the value the legend tells laid out by its kind:
      the head beside the gloss of the page `doc` reads of the value, each
      part its kind reads by a key or an index on a line of its own beside
      the gloss of its page, a part at an index named beside it, and every
      comment closed and whitespace, so the text reads back as the value
      told.
      ::link~(::any/legend | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ The print of the value told, laid out. ~~| ::string
    | proves :glossesEachPartItsKindWires
        |~~ A part its kind wires stands beside the gloss of its page and the
            name that reads it.
        ~~|
        ~(::point[0 1 2] | legend | print | lines | get /2 | contains "|~ The line of the point, counted from one · line ~|")
    | impl ::builtin{}
